```
$ jci-audit verify -h
Re-verify a past release against its recorded advisory snapshot

Usage: jci-audit verify [OPTIONS] --release-version <VERSION>

Options:
      --release-version <VERSION>  The released version to verify (e.g. "1.2.0")
  -v, --verbose...                 Increase logging verbosity
      --advisory-db <ADVISORY_DB>  Advisory-db root; the checkout is moved to the recorded commit
  -q, --quiet...                   Decrease logging verbosity
      --owner <OWNER>              GitHub repository owner that published the release (e.g. "jerus-org")
      --repo <REPO>                GitHub repository name that published the release (e.g. "jci-audit")
      --tag-prefix <TAG_PREFIX>    Release tag prefix (e.g. "jci-audit-v"); combined with --release-version to form the tag to fetch
      --deny-warnings              Fail if the tools report any warning
  -h, --help                       Print help (see more with '--help')

$ jci-audit verify --help
Re-verify a past release against its recorded advisory snapshot.

Uses the policy (deny.toml) that was in force at the time. Run it from a checkout of the released tag.

Usage: jci-audit verify [OPTIONS] --release-version <VERSION>

Options:
      --release-version <VERSION>
          The released version to verify (e.g. "1.2.0")

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity

      --advisory-db <ADVISORY_DB>
          Advisory-db root; the checkout is moved to the recorded commit.
          
          Defaults to ~/.cargo/advisory-db.

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease logging verbosity

      --owner <OWNER>
          GitHub repository owner that published the release (e.g. "jerus-org").
          
          Required by the remote-fetch fallback (no local record found); ignored when verifying from a checkout.

      --repo <REPO>
          GitHub repository name that published the release (e.g. "jci-audit").
          
          Only used by the remote-fetch fallback.

      --tag-prefix <TAG_PREFIX>
          Release tag prefix (e.g. "jci-audit-v"); combined with --release-version to form the tag to fetch.
          
          Only used by the remote-fetch fallback.

      --deny-warnings
          Fail if the tools report any warning

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

```
